Origin

devflow is the Devflow engine of devpit (https://github.com/jholhewres/devpit,
Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026 Jhol Hewres), made to run on its own.
Code is extracted from devpit at commit 7153771; devpit's history keeps how it
got there.

The skills, reviewer personas, findings schema and rubrics that come with that
code are adapted from MIT- and Apache-2.0-licensed sources. Their notices are
added here, verbatim from devpit's NOTICE, in the same commit that brings them.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Devflow skills

The skills under flow/skills/, the reviewer personas under flow/personas/ and
the findings schema in flow/schemas/devflow-findings.schema.json are devpit's
own text, adapted from the sources below. Their evals follow the pattern of
anthropics/skills' skill-creator.

  flow/skills/devflow-briefing      grilling, grill-me; interview-me
  flow/skills/devflow-context       to-spec, domain-modeling; spec-driven-development
  flow/skills/devflow-plan          to-tickets; planning-and-task-breakdown
  flow/skills/devflow-execution     tdd, diagnosing-bugs; test-driven-development,
                                    incremental-implementation
  flow/skills/devflow-review        code-review; code-review-and-quality,
                                    security-and-hardening; requesting-code-review
  flow/skills/devflow-completion    handoff; verification-before-completion
  flow/skills/devflow-setup         devpit's own
  flow/personas/devflow-spec        agents/code-reviewer; code-review
  flow/personas/devflow-standards   agents/code-reviewer; code-review
  flow/personas/devflow-security    agents/security-auditor; security-and-hardening

